From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Thu, 08 Oct 2026 06:32:50 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: use RCU link lookups in net_fill_forward_path

mac80211 calls the forward path op under the RCU read lock, without
the device mutex. The driver reads the vif link of the station with a
lookup whose lockdep check requires that mutex. If the default link
of the station is not link 0, lockdep reports suspicious RCU usage.
The read also lacks the dependency ordering of an RCU read.

Read the vif link with an RCU accessor, as the station link lookup
already does. Slot 0 of the vif link table holds the embedded vif
link, so the result for link 0 does not change. Read the default link
ID once and check its range, because link removal changes it under
the mutex. Both lookups then use the same link ID.

Fixes: 377aa17d2aed ("wifi: mt76: mt7996: Add NPU offload support to MT7996 driver")
Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 mt7996/main.c |   10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/mt7996/main.c
+++ b/mt7996/main.c
@@ -3352,17 +3352,23 @@ mt7996_net_fill_forward_path(struct ieee
 			     struct net_device_path_ctx *ctx,
 			     struct net_device_path *path)
 {
+	struct mt7996_vif *mvif = (struct mt7996_vif *)vif->drv_priv;
 	struct mt7996_sta *msta = (struct mt7996_sta *)sta->drv_priv;
 	struct mt7996_dev *dev = mt7996_hw_dev(hw);
 	struct mtk_wed_device *wed = &dev->mt76.mmio.wed;
+	u8 link_id = READ_ONCE(msta->deflink_id);
 	struct mt7996_sta_link *msta_link;
 	struct mt7996_vif_link *link;
 
-	link = mt7996_vif_link(dev, vif, msta->deflink_id);
+	if (link_id >= IEEE80211_MLD_MAX_NUM_LINKS)
+		return -EIO;
+
+	link = (struct mt7996_vif_link *)
+	       rcu_dereference(mvif->mt76.link[link_id]);
 	if (!link)
 		return -EIO;
 
-	msta_link = mt7996_sta_link(msta, msta->deflink_id);
+	msta_link = mt7996_sta_link(msta, link_id);
 	if (!msta_link)
 		return -EIO;
 
